            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policies</strong><br>\nFrederick focused on domestic affairs when not engaged in warfare. He worked on the improvement of the Prussian economy by encouraging trade and agriculture. He invited immigrants to settle in Prussia to increase the population and workforce. Moreover, he established a system of merit for hiring civil servants, reducing corruption and improving government efficiency.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legal Reforms</strong><br>\nOne of his significant contributions was the reform of the Prussian legal system. He abolished torture and made the laws simpler and more humane. This reformation process created a more centralized and efficient system of justice that served as a model for other European nations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Philosophical and Cultural Achievements</strong><br>\nFrederick was a patron of the arts and an accomplished musician and writer himself. He maintained correspondence with prominent philosophers like Voltaire. His court was a European hub for culture and philosophy, reflecting the enlightenment ideals he sought to incorporate into his rule.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
